%C - QNX sample application

Syntax:
%C [argument ...]

Arguments:
Any arguments are accepted. They are echoed back one per line and then
summarised.

Description:
A small QNX Neutrino application whose only job is to report on the context
it was started in. It prints, in order:

    a banner
    the full path it was loaded from, as reported by _cmdname()
    the current working directory
    its arguments, one per line
    length statistics for those arguments
    the environment it inherited

Build options:
Options are make variables, set on the make command line or from a CLion
build configuration, not runtime arguments:

    SHOW_ENV=1          include the environment dump (default 0, omitted)

Build variants:
The recursive build walks Makefile -> nto -> <cpu> -> <variant>, producing one
binary per target CPU and build type. The debug variants are built without
optimisation and keep the "_g" suffix, so they can sit on a target alongside
the release build:

    nto/x86_64/o          qnx-sample      x86_64, optimised
    nto/x86_64/o-g        qnx-sample_g    x86_64, debug
    nto/aarch64/o.le      qnx-sample      aarch64 little-endian, optimised
    nto/aarch64/o.le-g    qnx-sample_g    aarch64 little-endian, debug

Exit status:
 0      Success.
